            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Lower Mainland–Southwest</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$20.00</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$23.50</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$29.75</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Vancouver Island and Coast</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$19.00</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$24.00</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$30.00</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Thompson–Okanagan</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$19.00</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$22.60</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$30.00</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Northeast</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$19.31</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$22.67</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$33.45</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Kootenay</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$18.25</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$22.00</td><td class="px-4 py-3">$33.30</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Hourly wages, updated by Job Bank on November 19, 2025.</p>

      <p>
        Many B.C. centres also pay the province's <strong>ECE Wage Enhancement</strong> of up to $6 an hour to eligible certified ECEs. Its 2026–27 funding guidelines list ECE Assistants as ineligible. One caution: the BC PNP scores only your hourly wage and excludes bonuses and "other similar payments." The program guide does not mention the wage enhancement specifically, so ask the BC PNP (PNPInfo@gov.bc.ca) before you claim points for it, and make sure the wage written in your job offer matches what you actually receive.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Other eligibility requirements</h2>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
        <li><strong>Work experience:</strong> at least two years of full-time (or equivalent) experience in any TEER 0–3 occupation within the last ten years, in Canada or abroad. Work done on a study permit does not count, except paid, full-time co-op terms in a skilled occupation, and only once you have completed your program.</li>
        <li><strong>Language:</strong> NOC 42202 is a TEER 2 occupation, so you need at least CLB 4 in all four skills on CELPIP-General, IELTS General Training, PTE Core, TEF Canada or TCF Canada.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal status:</strong> you cannot be out of status or working without authorization in Canada.</li>
        <li><strong>Minimum income:</strong> your family income in B.C. must meet the program's minimum, which is based on Statistics Canada's low-income cut-off. For a single person it is $31,264 in Metro Vancouver and $26,057 elsewhere in B.C.; for a family of three, $47,851 and $39,878. A full-time ECE at the provincial median of $24.00 an hour earns about $49,900 a year at 40 hours a week.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Every 2026 Childcare draw</h2>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-8">
        <table class="min-w-full border border-slate-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-bold text-slate-700">Date</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-bold text-slate-700">Minimum score</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-bold text-slate-700">Invitations</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
